  "lineage": "Early-1990s American indie rock substyle characterized by deliberately-loose performance aesthetic, lo-fi production, deadpan vocal delivery, and oblique-fragmentary lyrical content. Pavement (Stockton, 1989-1999) is the canonical type-specimen; parallel acts include Sebadoh, Guided by Voices, Silver Jews, and Built to Spill. Distinguished from broader indie rock by slacker rock's explicit casual-attitudinal aesthetic and emphasis on rough-edged production.",
